\ChangesListline {added}{Added\nobreakspace {}(revproof)}{This section frames the motivation and scope of the work. We first identify the core research problem and the limitations of existing approaches that motivate it. We then summarise the main contributions of the proposed solution, and conclude with the research questions that structure the experimental evaluation.}{1}
\ChangesListline {replaced}{Replaced\nobreakspace {}(rev)}{artificial intelligence}{1}
\ChangesListline {replaced}{Replaced\nobreakspace {}(rev)}{KT traditional models}{2}
\ChangesListline {added}{Added\nobreakspace {}(revproof)}{This subsection details the evaluation methodology developed to address each research question. We describe the metrics and protocols for quantifying the performance--interpretability trade-off (Section\nobreakspace {}\ref {sec:rq1_method}), the triple-validation approach for verifying the pedagogical grounding of internal representations (Section\nobreakspace {}\ref {sec:rq2_method}), and the comparative analysis strategy for evaluating context-aware personalisation capabilities (Section\nobreakspace {}\ref {sec:rq3_method}).}{13}
\ChangesListline {added}{Added\nobreakspace {}(revproof)}{This section presents and discusses the experimental results in correspondence with the three research questions. Section\nobreakspace {}\ref {sec_tradeoff} quantifies the accuracy--interpretability trade-off across benchmark datasets. Section\nobreakspace {}\ref {sec_grounded} assesses the pedagogical grounding of the model's internal representations through the triple-validation protocol. Section\nobreakspace {}\ref {sec_gran_results} evaluates the model's capacity to deliver context-aware personalised predictions.}{15}
